# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neuroglyphics — your vault is yours.
#
# This repo doubles as a vault template: once you clone it, this folder
# IS your vault. Everything is ignored by default — only the engine and
# its docs are tracked — so the clone stays a clean copy of the engine
# and `git pull` never has to fight your cards.
#
# Backing your vault up to your OWN private repo instead? Delete the
# lone "*" line below so everything becomes trackable again, then
# `git remote set-url origin …` to a repo you own and keep it private.
# Never push a tracked state.json to a public fork: it holds your salt.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Ignore everything by default...
*

# ...except the engine and its docs.
!.gitignore
!README.md
!neuroglyphics.py

# Obsidian workspace config — machine-specific, even in a private repo.
.obsidian/

# OS and editor cruft — same.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
